# __TEAM_REPO__ — operator orientation

**Template source: `agent-tooling/scaffold/team-repo-README.template`** (PROJ-039/T-095).
Team repos are not a `scaffold.sh` target today, so this file is placed **manually,
once**, by the team lead when the repo is created (see "Placement" at the bottom of
this file for the recommended mechanism) — it is not TOOLING_UPDATE-synced the way a
home repo's README is. If the template changes upstream, re-copy and re-substitute by
hand; there's no drift check for this one yet.

This file is for **you, the operator** — where to look, not how the team lead works.
Team-lead operating instructions live in each lead's home-repo `OPERATING-MANUAL.md`;
this README never duplicates them.

## What this repo is

`__TEAM_REPO__` is the **__TEAM__ team's** durable planning surface — shared state that
outlives any individual session or agent. It is distinct from any agent's **home repo**
(their session lifecycle, hooks, results) and from a **working repo** (a task repo an
agent clones into `.workspace/` to do briefed work). Only the team lead writes the
planning surface here; other agents interact with it only via the drafts channel
(below).

## Who writes here

- **The team lead** (`__TEAM__` lead) — the only writer of `planning/`. Direct commits
  to this repo's default branch, per the change-visibility policy below.
- **Any team agent** — may drop a draft handoff under `team/{recipient}/incoming/
  drafts/`, addressed to another agent on the team. The recipient (or the lead, at
  consolidation) reconciles it — promote, merge, or reject; never silently delete.
- **Another team's lead** — cross-team coordination lands here only via the drafts
  channel or an inter-team-lead brief, never a direct planning edit.

## Directory structure

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `planning/team-tasklist.md` | The team's task board — chronological, lead-owned. |
| `planning/STATUS.md` | Rolled-up status digest, rewritten at each consolidation pass. |
| `planning/sessions/active.md` | Session registry — one row per in-flight/recent agent session, lead-owned. |
| `planning/projects/` | Per-project planning docs (multi-task initiatives). |
| `team/{agent}/incoming/drafts/` | Cross-team / cross-agent handoff inbox — drafts awaiting reconciliation. |
| `agenticflows/` | Team conventions, role specs, operations docs — the "how we work" reference material. |

## How agent activity is recorded — where this repo fits in the trail

This repo does not host session commits or results — those live in each agent's own
**home repo** (`results/session-*.md`). What lands here is the **consolidated view**:
the team lead's `/consolidate-tasks` pass reads each agent's results/telemetry and
writes the summary into `planning/sessions/active.md`, `planning/team-tasklist.md`, and
`planning/STATUS.md`. If you want raw session detail, start at the agent's home repo;
if you want the team-wide status picture, start here.

## The change-visibility policy — which changes arrive as a PR, and which don't

Decided 2026-07-10; applies fleet-wide:

- **Home repos** — agent sessions are hook-managed: push to the default branch
  **directly, no PR**.
- **Team repos** (this repo) — the team lead's own adjustments to its own team repo
  push to the default branch **directly, no PR** (this generalises what used to be an
  apex-only privilege to every lead, on their own team repo).
- **Working repos** — any repo checked out under a session's `.workspace/` and modified
  per a brief's instructions (including when that repo happens to be a home or team
  repo, because the brief specifically targeted it) goes through the **PR path**. These
  are not operational hook-driven changes — they're briefed work product.
- **Rare exception:** a brief or operator instruction can explicitly target the CURRENT
  operational team/home repo you're standing on ("re-engineering the beam we are
  standing on"). **Caveat:** any change made this way to an agent-tooling **manifest
  item** (a file `sync-agent-tooling.sh` manages) is overwritten on the next
  `TOOLING_UPDATE` — such a change is not durable unless it also lands as an
  agent-tooling PR.

In short: if you see a commit straight on this repo's default branch by the team lead,
that's the policy working as designed, not a bypassed review. A PR against this repo
means an agent was specifically briefed to modify it as working-repo content.

## Placement (this template is not scaffold-emitted)

Team repos aren't created by `scaffold.sh`, so there's no automatic emission point for
this README yet. Recommended mechanism until one exists: the team lead copies this
template to `README.md` at the team repo root once, at team stand-up time (or
retroactively for an existing team repo), substituting `__TEAM__` and `__TEAM_REPO__`
by hand. Treat this template file as the canonical source for any future edits — don't
hand-drift the copies across teams; re-copy from here instead. Wiring an automatic sync
target for team repos (mirroring the home-repo TOOLING_UPDATE mechanism) was
deliberately deferred out of this change.
